<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hoshang Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1435</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Alp Khan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hoshang Shah was the second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>, reigning from 1406 to 1435, son of the dynasty's founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilawar-khan-ghuri">Dilawar Khan Ghuri</a>. He moved the capital from Dhar to the hill fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandu">Mandu</a>, which he fortified, and fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> states. His marble tomb at Mandu is considered the earliest marble building in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hoshang-shah.jpg" alt="Hoshang Shah" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drnsreedhar1959 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:001hoshang-1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
